**You need:** an existing class to put the student in — see
[Add a Class](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-class) — and permission to create students.

## Steps

1. Open **Students → Classes** and open the class the student is joining.
2. Select **Add Student**. (You can also reach the same form from **Students → Student Search**.)
3. Fill in the form. The fields you see depend on your institute (see below), but these are the ones
   that behave specially:
   - **Student ID** — required, digits only, and **unique across the institute**. If the ID is
     already taken the field tells you so as you type. You cannot change it later by editing the
     student, so decide your numbering scheme before you start enrolling.
   - **RFID** — the number on the student's attendance card. Also digits only, also checked for
     duplicates. Leave it empty if cards are issued later; attendance simply won't scan until it is
     filled in.
   - **Student's Full Name** — letters, spaces and full stops only.
   - **Date of Birth** — a date picker, stored as `YYYY-MM-DD`.
   - **Class** — pre-filled with the class you came from. Like Student ID, it is read-only once the
     student exists; moving a student between classes is a separate action, not an edit.
   - **Contact Number** — optional, but attendance SMS and payment reminders go to this number, so a
     student with no number silently receives nothing.
4. Add a **photo** if your institute uses them — this is what appears on
   [ID cards](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-id-cards) and in class lists.
5. If the student has a **sibling** already enrolled, use the sibling picker to link them. Search by
   Student ID or name. Sibling links are what family discounts key off.
6. Select **Save**.

## Why your form looks different from the screenshots

The Add Student form is **configured per institute**. Which fields exist, which are required, what
they are labelled, and what they will accept all come from your institute's own field definition —
which is why one school asks for NIC number, house and ethnicity while another asks for none of them.

Two consequences worth knowing:

- If a field you need is missing, it can be switched on for your institute. It is a configuration
  change, not a new feature.
- A field marked optional here may be marked required at your institute, and vice versa.

## Editing and removing

Open the student from **Students → Student Search** or from the class roster. Everything is editable
except **Student ID** and **Class**. **Delete Student** asks for confirmation and removes the record
outright — for a student who has simply left, prefer whatever your institute's leaving process is
over deleting, because deleting takes their attendance and results history with them.

